# Everything not excluded here is copied into the image by `COPY . .` in the build
# stage, then carried into the runtime stage and pushed to a registry.

# The credential, first and loudest. A built image is pushed to a registry and run on a
# public host, so a .env baked into it is a published secret, not a local one.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Host node_modules are built for the developer's platform. `COPY . .` runs *after* the
# Dockerfile copies the deps stage's modules, so without this the macOS build of
# better-sqlite3 silently overwrites the Linux one compiled against this image's Node
# ABI — a build that succeeds and a container that cannot open the ledger.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# The hash chain belongs to the deployment's mounted volume. Shipping a developer's
# ledger would start every deploy carrying someone else's blocks.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# Rebuilt inside the image by `npm run build`.
.next
**/.next

# Not needed to run the service, and large.
.git
.github
.recording
*.mp4
*.pdf

.DS_Store
npm-debug.log*
*.log
